        'en' => [
            'title'   => 'Laser cut Christmas ornaments and gifts: ideas and machines',
            'slug'    => 'laser-cut-christmas-ornaments-gifts',
            'excerpt' => 'Learn how to make laser cut Christmas ornaments and gifts, which plywood and xTool machine to choose, and how to plan the busy season in good time.',
            'blocks'  => [
                [ 'p', 'The easiest way to start with laser cut Christmas ornaments is 3 mm plywood: a diode laser cuts baubles, stars and gift tags from it, and engraving adds a name or a year. For colourful ornaments without painting, use the xTool M2 with CMYK printing; for large batches from full sheets, the xTool P3 CO₂ laser; and for glass and crystal, the xTool F2 Ultra UV. Start preparing by early November at the latest, with samples, templates and a production plan.' ],
                [ 'p', 'In the run-up to Christmas markets, Secret Santa swaps and office parties, customers look for small, personal gifts, and companies order engraved presents for their clients. Below you will find product ideas, materials, machine choices and a season plan for a small workshop.' ],
                [ 'h2', 'Laser cut Christmas ornaments and gifts: product ideas' ],
                [ 'ul', [
                    'Plywood baubles with names: flat baubles, stars and hearts with a name, a year or a short message.',
                    'Layered stars and snowflakes: two or three layers of plywood glued together, or fretwork snowflakes and slot-together trees.',
                    'Gift tags: plywood, card or felt with the recipient’s name. After Christmas, they stay on the tree.',
                    'Advent calendars: houses with little drawers or boards with 24 doors, made from 3–6 mm plywood.',
                    'Engraved glassware and drinkware: wine glasses, tumblers, crystal ornaments and travel mugs with a name or company logo.',
                    'Metal ornaments and keyrings: anodised aluminium and steel with a date or initials.',
                    'Slate coasters: a light engraving on dark stone, for example a set with a winter motif and the family name.',
                    'Packaging: plywood boxes with a logo, fretwork card boxes, labels and inserts.',
                ] ],
                [ 'p', 'We cover slate engraving, tumblers and paper cutting in more detail in separate articles.' ],
                [ 'h2', 'Which materials work for laser cut Christmas ornaments?' ],
                [ 'h3', 'Plywood: thickness and type' ],
                [ 'p', 'For tree ornaments, 3 mm plywood is the standard: light, stiff and quick to cut. xTool sells birch and basswood plywood in this thickness in 30 × 30 cm sheets but check compatibility with your specific machine and laser module before buying. Keep 4–6 mm plywood for standing decorations and advent calendars; a diode laser cuts it in several passes, a CO₂ laser faster.' ],
                [ 'p', 'Birch is pale and hard and gives a high-contrast engraving, while basswood is lighter and easier for fine patterns. Buy plywood made for lasers: construction and exterior-grade plywood has thicker glue layers and voids where the cut does not go through. MDF takes paint well, but its edges come out dark.' ],
                [ 'h3', 'Acrylic, felt and card' ],
                [ 'p', 'Mirror, gold or clear acrylic makes striking stars and lettering. Clear acrylic is cut with a CO₂ laser, because the blue beam of a diode laser passes through it. Felt and card are good for soft tags and packaging.' ],
                [ 'h3', 'Painting and sealing' ],
                [ 'ul', [
                    'Masking tape: xTool recommends taping plywood before processing to reduce darkening from the laser.',
                    'Painting through the mask: engrave the design through the tape, fill it with acrylic or spray paint, and only then peel off the tape. The colour stays only in the recesses.',
                    'Sealing: clear acrylic varnish, oil or wax. On M2 prints, apply varnish thinly, ideally as a spray, after testing it on a sample.',
                    'Finishing touches: twine, ribbon or gold paint on the edge. xTool’s 3 mm basswood rounds come with ready-made holes and twine for hanging.',
                ] ],
                [ 'h2', 'Which machine for which Christmas product?' ],
                [ 'h3', 'Colourful ornaments without painting: xTool M2' ],
                [ 'p', 'The M2 combines a 10, 20 or 40 W diode laser with a CMYK inkjet module, available in the Color Print & Cut bundle or as an add-on. According to xTool, the M2 ink prints in full colour on paper, wood, acrylic and fabric. The machine prints the design and the laser cuts the outline, so a colourful bauble or magnet is made without a brush. Two cameras with live preview help you place the design, and the enclosed design meets Class 1.' ],
                [ 'p', 'The CleanCut panel protects the base plate when cutting through and, according to xTool, supports card, sticker paper, felt and thin leather. The M2 is a craft machine for short runs; large batches from full sheets are better done on the P3.' ],
                [ 'products', '15452856942805,9570646196437' ],
                [ 'h3', 'Wood and names: xTool F2 and S1' ],
                [ 'p', 'The F2 has a 15 W diode laser and a 5 W IR laser, and its 50 MP camera helps position designs. It can personalise ornaments and metal keyrings in an appropriately prepared workshop. The manufacturer does not permit public use of the F2. Choose the S1 or P3 for cutting ornaments from full sheets.' ],
                [ 'p', 'The S1 is an enclosed Class 1 diode laser with a 20 or 40 W module and a 608 × 385 mm bed, enough for a whole batch of baubles or advent calendar parts. It has flame detection from five directions and a lid-open safety stop. It cuts thick boards in several passes, and it cannot cut clear acrylic.' ],
                [ 'products', '9163846877397,8169201631445' ],
                [ 'h3', 'Batches from large sheets: xTool P3' ],
                [ 'p', 'The P3 is an 80 W CO₂ laser with a 914 × 457 mm bed and speeds of up to 1,200 mm/s. Four cameras help you lay out parts on the sheet, and the ACS™ workflow sets positioning and focus automatically. It also cuts clear and mirror acrylic and thicker plywood for advent calendars. With the intelligent conveyor feeder, the working area grows to 610 × 1300 mm. The P3 needs space and fume extraction to the outside, though; for a few dozen name ornaments, a diode laser is enough.' ],
                [ 'p', 'According to xTool, the P3 with its conveyor is a Class 4 laser. It requires trained operators, a designated laser safety officer who operates the device or directs its use, a controlled area and the safeguards specified in the manual, including goggles rated for 10.6 µm laser radiation. Do not use it in public or around untrained people or children. The Auto Streamline conveyor works only with Class 4 versions of the F1 Ultra, F2 Ultra and F2 Ultra UV. Its use requires a controlled area and protection selected according to the device manual.' ],
                [ 'products', '9089720189141,9089525088469' ],
                [ 'h3', 'Glass, crystal and wine glasses: xTool F2 Ultra UV' ],
                [ 'p', 'The F2 Ultra UV has a 5 W UV laser for engraving glass, crystal, ceramics, acrylic, metal and wood. Results depend on the material and settings, so test first. It has two 48 MP cameras and, according to xTool, can engrave 3D designs inside suitable crystal.' ],
                [ 'p', 'Wine glasses, mugs and spheres need a rotary attachment. The RA3 has roller, chuck, sphere and ring modes; it works with the P3, F2 and F2 Ultra UV, and the RA3 Lite version with the M2. Glass baubles are thin and fragile, so keep spares for testing. The F2 Ultra UV is not meant for cutting plywood ornaments in batches.' ],
